# Predicting Smartphone Addiction

Playground Series - Season 6 Episode 8

**Evaluation metric:** Roc Auc Score
**Data** (read-only, in `/data`):
- `sample_submission.csv`: 296302 rows; columns: id, addicted_label
- `test.csv`: 296302 rows; columns: id, age, daily_screen_time_hours, social_media_hours, gaming_hours, work_study_hours, sleep_hours, notifications_per_day, app_opens_per_day, weekend_screen_time, gender, stress_level, academic_work_impact
- `train.csv`: 691369 rows; columns: id, age, daily_screen_time_hours, social_media_hours, gaming_hours, work_study_hours, sleep_hours, notifications_per_day, app_opens_per_day, weekend_screen_time, gender, stress_level, academic_work_impact, addicted_label

**Deliverable:** write `/work/submission.csv` in exactly the format of `/data/sample_submission.csv` (same ids, same
columns). Only the file present at the end counts.

**Rules of this run**
- Time limit: 60 minutes of wall clock; the run is stopped at the limit. Budget your experiments.
- There is no internet access. Python packages already installed are all you have (pandas, numpy, scikit-learn,
  lightgbm, xgboost, catboost, scipy, optuna). Library documentation: `python -c "help(...)"`.
- One research tool is available: the `arxiv` MCP tool (search and read papers submitted before 2026-08-01).
- Work in `/work`. CPU only (4 cores, 16 GB RAM).
